## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design extensible text processing with runtime plugins, without touching core; demonstrates a clean separation of concerns and Open/Closed compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Pipeline/Chain of Responsibility pattern
- Runtime registry for extensibility
- Minimal transform interface and composition order
- Deterministic, idempotent transforms

## Code Example

```javascript
class Transform {
  constructor(name, fn) { this.name = name; this.fn = fn; }
  apply(text) { return this.fn(text); }
}
class Registry {
  constructor(){ this.factories = new Map(); }
  register(name, factory){ this.factories.set(name, factory); }
  create(name){ const f = this.factories.get(name); return f ? f() : null; }
}
class Pipeline {
  constructor(registry, names){ this.transforms = names.map(n => registry.create(n)).filter(t => t); }
  run(input){ return this.transforms.reduce((acc, t) => t.apply(acc), input); }
}

const registry = new Registry();
registry.register('trim', () => new Transform('trim', s => s.trim()));
registry.register('collapseSpaces', () => new Transform('collapseSpaces', s => s.replace(/\s+/g, ' ')));
registry.register('toUpper', () => new Transform('toUpper', s => s.toUpperCase()));

const names = ['trim','collapseSpaces','toUpper'];
const pipeline = new Pipeline(registry, names);
console.log(pipeline.run('  hello   world  ')); // 'HELLO WORLD'
```

